NAME
     cmp - compare two files byte by byte

SYNOPSIS
     cmp [-s] [-l] FILE1 [FILE2]

DESCRIPTION
     cmp says where two files first differ, and nothing at all when they
     are the same. FILE2 may be left out, or either name may be -, to
     mean standard input.

OPTIONS
     -s   say nothing; the exit status is the answer
     -l   list every differing byte, with both values in octal

SEE ALSO
     diff(1), md5 is not provided
